<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.9% week to Aug 14.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.9% week to Aug 14.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.9 percent in the week to August 13 over the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said on Thursday. Last week the rise was 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>(Figures in rounded billions of stg)</p>
<p>			Latest week   Previous wk   Year-ago wk</p>
<p>Notes in circulation  22.10	   22.10	   20.87</p>
<p>Bankers deposits	 2.56	    2.51	    1.88</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
